{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786210148,"nonce":"WR8LzZai3j/s2VJda7ZtaBCCPIw=","target":"f7063f7355ff842adfd9406e6e69d65fc590930031a42bc817797a7a6369cab1","message":"**What is wrong.** There is no way to prove oto's notification path works without\nwaiting for a real alert. `POST /api/v1/channels/{id}/test` exists\n(`internal/channels/api/ports.go:71` — \"sends one synthetic alert card\") but it\nshort-circuits everything that matters: it renders one card and calls the\nprovider directly. It does not go through ingestion, alert identity, grouping,\nthe notification policy match, the rule snapshot, `channel_threads` sequencing,\nthe ordering gate, `reply_broadcast`, or the delivery record.\n\n**Why it matters.** The owner asked for a UI action that pushes a synthetic alert\nthrough the *real* pipeline. A scope check (\"do I have `chat:write`?\") answers a\nquestion nobody has; \"will an alert actually reach my channel, in a thread, with\nthe right card, and be recorded?\" is the question an operator has on day one, and\ntoday the only way to answer it is to break something in production. Every\nfailure mode oto has — a policy that matches nothing, a thread that will not open,\na scope Slack silently ignores, a renderer that produces an invalid block — is\ninvisible until the first real page.\n\n**Where.** New: a `test alert` action in `web/src/features/settings/` (or the\nsources screen), an endpoint alongside `internal/channels/api/`, driving\n`internal/ingestion/service/accept.go` with a synthetic Alertmanager payload so\nthe whole chain runs.\n\n**Done when.** One click in the UI produces: an alert row marked as synthetic, a\ngroup, a rendered card in the target Slack channel in a real thread, a\n`notification_deliveries` row, and a result screen that names the stage that\nfailed when it fails. The synthetic alert is distinguishable and disposable — it\nmust not pollute alert quality stats or the history the product is selling.","files":null}]}